{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["And the reason for <b>but I will remember for them the covenant of the first ones</b> is that I will remember for them thus, both in the land and outside the land in the exile hinted at here, and likewise in all generations. And this is the reason for 'before the eyes of the nations' (לעיני הגויים), for He will act on their behalf for the sake of His great Name, so that it not be profaned among the nations, and not for their sake, for they did not repent and their iniquities were not atoned. And thus our Rabbis said (Sifra, ch. 8:10): 'I have not rejected them (לא מאסתים)' — in the days of Vespasian; 'nor have I abhorred them (ולא געלתים)' — in the days of Greece; 'to destroy them, to break My covenant with them (לכלותם להפר בריתי אתם)' — in the days of Haman; 'for I am YHWH their Elohim (כי אני ה׳ אלהיהם)' — in the days of Gog and Magog.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:01:04.561800769Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}